# The keys whose signature makes a Seamless release: an OpenSSH
# allowed_signers file (ssh-keygen(1), ALLOWED SIGNERS). The owner signs each
# release's checksums.txt with one of them, on a hardware security key, in
# the namespace seamless-release:
#
#   ssh-keygen -Y sign -n seamless-release -f <key handle> checksums.txt
#
# (scripts/release/sign.sh runs it, as checksums.txt.sshsig.) The release
# workflow publishes a release only once that signature verifies against
# this file as it was at the previous release's tag and as it is at the
# release's own: a key added here signs from the next release on, and a key
# removed here stops signing at this one (scripts/release/README.md).
# docs/install and docs/install.ps1 carry a copy of these lines, which
# scripts/site-check.sh holds to this file.
#
# One line per key: principal, namespaces="seamless-release", key. Never add
# verify-required (ssh-keygen refuses the line); the verifiers require user
# verification from the signature's flags instead. A fork that signs its own
# releases lists its own keys here.
